  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish several important ingredients: the closely related AlCoCrFeNi2.1 eutectic alloy has an FCC/B2 lamellar structure (R3, R9, R12); thermal processing can alter phase constitution and decomposition length scales in related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloys (R7, R8, R19); and, most importantly, coherent or hierarchical precipitate structures can transmit dislocations, relieve stress concentrations, suppress cracking, and improve strength–ductility combinations in HEAs (R2, R6, R16). Pressure-induced phase transformation in a related HEA and high-pressure torsion processing provide limited pressure-related precedent (R5, R10). Thus an expert could infer that converting brittle incoherent lamellae into a coherent hierarchical structure may be beneficial, but the specific use of combined high-pressure/high-temperature treatment in a hexahedron-anvil apparatus for Al0.7CoCrFeNi is not disclosed or strongly suggested and would require a substantial new processing idea."
}
